cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sc-report, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references (the methods of the steps whose results it reports, its own, and the demo datasets)."
type: software
title: sc-report
abstract: >-
  A Pennsieve processor, the last step of the single-cell workflows (Single-nucleus Atlas Mapping
  & Condition Comparison; Multiome Gene Regulation). It reads whatever upstream outputs it is
  given and writes one self-contained offline HTML report (samples, QC, clusters, cell types and
  composition, markers, differential expression, ATAC QC and regulatory results, methods, and the
  citations gathered from every step's provenance) and the tables behind it.
authors:
  - name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
repository-code: "https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/sc-report"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - single-nucleus
  - multiome
  - report
